{"id":"u-bb6095fc-d6e3-4334-960a-d5729e6bb766","src":"community","title":"Pookie Program: RELOADED","author":"","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/dOBMu0-pookie-program-reloaded","desc":"The Pookie Program RELOADED is a structured 13-week training system built around progressive overload, strategic fatigue management, and high-quality hypertrophy training. The program uses rotating movement patterns, varied intensity phases, and balanced volume distribution to continuously drive adaptation while minimizing burnout and stagnation.\n\nProgram breakdown\n\nWeeks 1–4: Foundation Phase\n\nWeeks 5–8: Hypertrophy Phase\n\nWeeks 9–12: Intensification Phase\n\nWeek 13: Deload and Recovery\n\n\nWeekly Structure \n\n* Monday — Legs A\n* Tuesday — Chest/Back A\n* Wednesday — Rest\n* Thursday — Shoulders/Arms\n* Friday — Legs B\n* Saturday — Chest/Back B\n* Sunday — Rest\n\nActive rest days are ideal (30 min max incline treadmill walk + stretching)\n\nIMPORTANT \n\nProgressive overloading \n\nEvery week:\n* add reps\n    OR\n* add weight\n    OR\n* improve execution\n\nEven tiny jumps count.\n\nSUPER SETS\n\nMovements listed as A and B  are to be supersetted with eachother\n\nREST TIMES\n\nHeavy compounds\n1-2 mins\n\nIsolation\n60-90 sec\n\nCalves/abs\n45-60 sec\n\nThe program prioritizes:\n\n* Upper chest development\n* Balanced posterior chain growth\n* Shoulder width and rear delt development\n* Functional strength progression\n* Sustainable recovery\n* Long-term hypertrophy without excessive junk volume\n\nBuilt for intermediate to advanced lifters, The Pookie Program combines compound strength work with targeted hypertrophy methods to create consistent, measurable physique and performance improvements over time.","level":["Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-03T18:02:22.226Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Legs A","Chest/Back A","Shoulders/Arms","Legs B","Chest/Back B"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":4}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}]},{"n":"Cable Crunch","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}],"note":"Single arm, sitting at a 45° angle. 10-12 reps each side"},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":10,"x":4}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}],"note":"Low-to-high"},{"n":"Straight Arm Pulldown","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Reverse Pec Deck","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}],"note":"15 reps each arm"},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":4}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"V-Handle Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":4}]}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Wrist Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":20,"x":4}],"note":"Bar behind back"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":20,"x":3}],"note":"10 each leg"},{"n":"Hip Adductor (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hip Abductor (Machine)","sets":[{"r":20,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"r":12,"x":4}]},{"n":"Good Morning","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}]},{"n":"Abs